               "Contributes to safer driving experiences, especially in challenging road conditions."
            ],
            "challenges": [
               "Achieving precise calibration of torque feedback across a wide range of vehicle speeds and steering angles.",
               "Maintaining system performance over time despite wear and environmental factors."
            ]
         }
      },
      {  
         "ID": 33,
         "text": "The vehicle control system must accurately monitor the yaw rate to ensure responsiveness to vehicle dynamics under various driving conditions.",
         "analysis": {
            "implications": [
               "Critical for stability control systems, aiding in preventing skids and loss of control.",
               "Supports advanced driver-assistance features like adaptive cruise control and lane-keeping assist."
            ],
            "challenges": [
               "Integrating yaw rate data with other vehicle dynamics information to make real-time adjustments.",
               "Ensuring sensor accuracy and reliability under diverse environmental conditions."
            ]
         }
      },
      {  
         "ID": 91,
         "text": "The Lane Keeping Assist system must maintain the vehicle's lane position within the road markings without driver input based on correlate sensing from both the steering angle sensor and the acceleration pedal sensor.",
         "analysis": {
            "implications": [
               "Improves safety by reducing the likelihood of unintentional lane departures.",
               "Relieves driver workload during long drives or in monotonous driving conditions."
            ],
            "challenges": [
               "Achieving high accuracy in lane detection and vehicle positioning, especially on poorly marked roads.",
               "Ensuring seamless integration between steering angle and acceleration pedal sensors for effective control."
            ]
         }
      },
